# Secrets for the Worker's server routes, in local development.
#
# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill in. `vp dev`, `vp preview` and
# `wrangler dev` load that file and bind each entry as a Worker secret;
# deployed, the same names are set with `wrangler secret put`.
#
# Nothing here is needed to run the app: the pages, the gene data and the
# in-browser optimizer need no secrets. Without these two, /api/mcp answers
# 503 (agent access is off) and /api/health answers liveness only.

# Named bearer tokens for the MCP endpoint at /api/mcp, which lets a
# scientist's own AI assistant search genes and run designs. Format:
# name:secret, comma separated. Each name appears in the logs and gets its own
# rate-limit budget, so one agent cannot spend another's and a design can be
# traced to its caller. Secrets must be at least 24 characters; generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 24
MCP_TOKENS=lab-agent:replace-me-with-at-least-24-characters

# Unlocks /api/health's deep check (a `head` of the corpus index in R2) for a
# caller presenting `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Anonymous probes always
# get liveness only.
HEALTH_AUTH_TOKEN=
